<h1>RichTextEditor</h1>

<p>
    The reactive editor component. It synchronizes changes from Quill back to Blazor after the configured
    debounce interval and can bind HTML, plain text, selection, enabled state, and touched state.
</p>

<h2 id="basic_usage">// basic_usage</h2>

<p>
    Bind <code>Content</code> to the HTML stored by your application. The basic toolbar is enabled by default.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="BasicEditorExample">
    <BasicEditorExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="content_and_events">// content_and_events</h2>

<p>
    <code>Content</code> contains HTML and is the primary value to persist. <code>Text</code> exposes the
    plain-text representation. <code>IsTouched</code> becomes true after an editor content change.
    <code>Selection</code> can also be bound when the current Quill range matters to your application.
    Content, text, and selection callbacks are throttled in JavaScript; change
    <code>DebounceIntervalInMilliseconds</code> when the 500 ms default does not suit your form.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="BindingsAndEventsExample">
    <BindingsAndEventsExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="themes_and_container_id">// themes_and_container_id</h2>

<p>
    Choose <code>QuillTheme.Snow</code> for a persistent toolbar or <code>QuillTheme.Bubble</code> for
    selection-driven formatting. Every editor receives a unique container id, but
    <code>EditorContainerHtmlId</code> lets you supply a stable one when integration or testing needs it.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="BubbleThemeExample">
    <BubbleThemeExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="enabled_state">// enabled_state</h2>

<p>
    Set or bind <code>IsEditorEnabled</code> to control whether content can be edited. A disabled toolbar
    remains visible by default. Set <code>ToolbarDisabledBehavior.Hidden</code> when it should disappear.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="EditorStateExample">
    <EditorStateExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="accessible_keybindings">// accessible_keybindings</h2>

<p>
    Quill normally uses Tab to indent the current line. Set <code>UseAccessibleKeybindings</code> to make
    Tab move focus out of the editor instead, which is usually preferable in forms. This option currently
    defaults to false for backwards compatibility.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="AccessibleKeybindingsExample">
    <AccessibleKeybindingsExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="toolbars">// toolbars</h2>

<p>
    The toolbar supports presets, custom controls, custom fonts, top or bottom placement, and a no-toolbar
    mode. See the <a href="guides/toolbars">toolbars guide</a> for live examples.
</p>
